PPC MP+sync+po
"Writer fenced, reader does two plain loads => isolates load->load reordering.
 Allowed by POWER (loads reorder freely), forbidden by PSO (loads stay ordered).
 This is the only direction that separates them: see README -- on the standard
 litmus families PSO turns out to be *included in* POWER (PSO has no behaviour
 POWER lacks), so the 'incomparable' label is generous."
{ 0:r2=x; 0:r4=y; 1:r2=y; 1:r4=x; }
 P0           | P1            ;
 li r1,1      | lwz r1,0(r2)  ;
 stw r1,0(r2) | lwz r3,0(r4)  ;
 sync         |               ;
 li r3,1      |               ;
 stw r3,0(r4) |               ;
exists (1:r1=1 /\ 1:r3=0)
